item.description:
Language is more than just a tool for communication—it&rsquo;s the bedrock of human thought and civilization.
The Sapir-Whorf Hypothesis The way we speak influences how we think&hellip;
Language and Power Words shape reality in profound ways.

Propaganda can be understood as a computational process that manipulates information flows.
Information as Input At its core, propaganda is about controlling what information reaches an audience&hellip;
Feedback Loops Modern propaganda systems create feedback loops that amplify certain narratives.
